        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 24 at 2:05PM CDT by NWS Amarillo TX</headline>
        <description>At 204 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 7
miles north of Glazier, or 8 miles south of Lipscomb, moving
northeast at 30 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Lipscomb, Higgins, and Glazier.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead to
localized flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.</instruction>
